    "summaryAr": "A private Family Office is seeking a licensed Helicopter Engineer to join a yacht-based VIP helicopter operation (Airbus ACH135), combining maintenance responsibility with an onboard safety-crew role. The Role Full line and base maintenance responsibility for the aircraft, onboard the yacht's support vessel Onboard safety-crew member, supporting the pilot during flight operations and in emergency scenarios Coordinati",
    "descriptionAr": "A private Family Office is seeking a licensed Helicopter Engineer to join a yacht-based VIP helicopter operation (Airbus ACH135), combining maintenance responsibility with an onboard safety-crew role. The Role Full line and base maintenance responsibility for the aircraft, onboard the yacht's support vessel Onboard safety-crew member, supporting the pilot during flight operations and in emergency scenarios Coordination with the aircraft's CAMO/continuing-airworthiness provider and the yacht's technical team Roster 3 weeks on / 3 weeks off, though in practice flexible around operational need — off time coordinated directly with the operating captain team rather than a rigid fixed pattern. Requirements EASA Part 66 (or UK CAA/GCAA equivalent) B1/B2 licence, valid type rating or ability to obtain one Significant helicopter maintenance experience; VIP, yacht-based or offshore operational background strongly preferred Additional safety-crew, hoist or rescue qualification an advantage Fluent English Based in Europe; flexible to reposition between the Mediterranean and Caribbean seasons Find Jobs in Switzerland on Arbeitnow",
